  "provider_query": "Public Telegram web preview of the official Telegram channel",
  "answer": "**Official channel public web preview:** [https://t.me/s/telegram](https://t.me/s/telegram) — **Telegram News** (@telegram), described as “The official Telegram on Telegram.”\n\n1. **[https://t.me/s/telegram](https://t.me/s/telegram)** — Official public web preview of @telegram (recent posts, no login). Source: Telegram web preview. [web:10]\n2. **[https://t.me/telegram](https://t.me/telegram)** — Channel landing page (join / open in app); preview is the `/s/` form above. Source: Telegram. [web:10]\n3. **Pattern: `https://t.me/s/<channel>`** — Public HTML preview of any public channel (about the latest ~20 posts; page back with `?before=<post-id>`). Source: Telegram public preview docs/usage notes. [web:1] [web:2] [web:9]\n4. **[https://telegram.org/blog](https://telegram.org/blog)** — Official product announcements site (not the channel feed itself). Source: Telegram Blog. [web:15]\n5. **[https://core.telegram.org/widgets/post](https://core.telegram.org/widgets/post)** — How to embed a public channel post from its `t.me` link. Source: Telegram Core. [web:7]\n6. **[https://tg.me/](https://tg.me/)** — Third-party browser layer over public Telegram (`t.me/name` → `tg.me/name`). Source: TG.ME. [web:0]\n7. **[https://opentg.ai/tools/telegram-channel-viewer](https://opentg.ai/tools/telegram-channel-viewer)** — Third-party viewer for public channels (latest posts only). Source: OpenTG. [web:8]\n8. **[https://anonytg.com/public-telegram-channel-viewer/](https://anonytg.com/public-telegram-channel-viewer/)** — Third-party public channel/post viewer that links back to Telegram. Source: AnonyTG. [web:4]\n\nFor the official channel only, use **https://t.me/s/telegram**. Third-party viewers are not operated by Telegram.",
